/**
 * T5 neighbourhood page — Saddle Club, north Midland, Midland County.
 *
 * The spine here is hydrology. Midland sits on the Llano Estacado, where playa
 * lakes are the defining drainage feature, and the city publishes its own
 * floodplain and playa mapping. Saddle Club is the one neighbourhood on this
 * site with named playas against its edge and a section literally called
 * "Lakes" inside mapped floodplain. That is a mosquito and occasional-invader
 * story no competitor page in this market is telling.
 *
 * VERIFIED facts used here, from the City of Midland's public ArcGIS
 * Subdivision layer (NAME, SURVEYOR, plat recording date, cabinet/page):
 *   FIVE separate plat families under the Saddle Club name, 22 plats:
 *    · Saddle Club "A"          1975-12-22  Kenneth E. Esmond   ← the oldest
 *    · Saddle Club South   1st  1977-03-10
 *                          2nd & 3rd 1978-11-14  Gary N. Haner
 *                          4th 1981-02-25 · 5th 1981-06-26 · 6th 1981-09-24
 *                          7th 1982-02-03 · 10th 1983-04-06 R. J. Eidson
 *                          11th 1985-05-15 · 12th 1998-12-08 · 13th 2002-08-21
 *                          (most surveyed by Max W. Richardson)
 *    · Saddle Club Estates      1981-06-17  Gary N. Haner  Cab C Pg 44-46
 *    · Saddle Club Lakes   2nd  1987-08-07 · 3rd 1994-05-19
 *    · Saddle Club East    1st  1989-11-17 · 2nd 1994-01-24 · 3rd 2005-01-05
 *                          4th 2007-07-23
 *    · Saddle Club Townhouse Area B  2nd 1989-03-13 · 3rd 1996-04-02
 *                          6th 2010-08-02   ← ATTACHED HOUSING EXISTS HERE
 *
 *  - Midland's public Drainage & Floodplain map service carries the 100-year
 *    and 500-year floodplain and a PLAYA attribute naming individual playas.
 *    Read Aug 2026: the centre of the Saddle Club LAKES plat area falls inside
 *    BOTH the mapped 100-year and 500-year floodplain. Named playa MI38 (base
 *    elevation 2,799 ft) has an extent overlapping the north-east corner of the
 *    Saddle Club plat area, and the MI41/MI42/MI43 playa cluster lies
 *    immediately north of its northern edge. The plat area CENTROID is not in
 *    floodplain — so this is an edges-and-margins situation, not a
 *    whole-neighbourhood one, and the page says exactly that.
 *  - THREE separate homeowners associations exist, which follows from the
 *    multiple plat families: Saddle Club South Homeowner's Association
 *    (clubhouse, pool, tennis courts, playground, published restrictions,
 *    bylaws and a violation-fines schedule); Saddle Club Owners Association,
 *    Inc. (management certificate on file with the state); and a Saddle Club
 *    Lake Addition association.
 *  - Midland County IS on the imported fire ant regulated-areas list under
 *    7 C.F.R. §301.81-3, adopted at 4 TAC §19.101.
 *
 * HOW TO PHRASE THE MAPPING — this matters:
 *  The floodplain and playa layers are the CITY'S OWN authoritative mapping.
 *  The statements about which plat areas they overlap are OUR reading of that
 *  mapping, computed from published extents. That is a sound method and it is
 *  still our reading, so the page tells people to check their own address
 *  against the city's map rather than trusting a pest control website for a
 *  floodplain determination. Never state a specific property is in floodplain.
 *
 * NOT ESTABLISHED — MUST NOT BE STATED:
 *  - Developer names. The city records SURVEYORS, who are not developers.
 *  - Acreage, lot counts, lot sizes, alleys, curbs, cul-de-sacs.
 *  - Which school serves it. Emerson Elementary and Goddard Junior High are
 *    roughly 0.8 miles south — that is proximity, not an attendance zone, and
 *    Midland ISD publishes zones only through a JavaScript tool we could not
 *    read. Say nothing about schools.
 *  - The contents of the Saddle Club Owners Association certificate. Located,
 *    not retrieved.
 *  - An earlier version of neighborhoods.ts called this "larger properties and
 *    more ground per home" with "outbuildings and equipment storage". No source
 *    supports that, and the documented townhouse plats cut against it. Removed.
 */
